5.1 Backend Development
The backend is developed using FastAPI.
FastAPI manages the requests from the frontend and connects each request to its respective module.
5.2 API Endpoints
EduGenie contains the following endpoints:
/qa
/explain
/quiz
/summarize
/learn/recommendations
Each endpoint is connected to its corresponding module logic. EduGenie-Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant_Document.docx
5.3 Explanation Module
The Explanation Module uses LaMini-Flan-T5 to provide concise and easy-to-understand explanations.
It is particularly useful for beginners and learners who have difficulty understanding complex concepts. EduGenie-Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant_Document.docx
5.4 Q&A Module
The Q&A module uses Gemini to answer general knowledge and academic questions.
It uses Gemini's contextual capabilities to provide AI-driven assistance to learners. EduGenie-Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant_Document.docx
5.5 Quiz Module
The Quiz Module generates three multiple-choice questions, with four options for each question.
The generated output is structured in JSON format for integration with the application. EduGenie-Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant_Document.docx
5.6 Summary Module
The Summary Module converts lengthy paragraphs into concise and easy-to-understand content while retaining important information. EduGenie-Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant_Document.docx
5.7 Learning Path Module
The Learning Path Module generates a structured learning path from beginner to advanced levels.
It can also suggest learning resources such as videos, articles and books. EduGenie-Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant_Document.docx
5.8 Frontend Development
The frontend contains:
Task dropdown
Text area
Submit button
Result container
Responsive styling
The available tasks include Explain, QnA, Quiz, Summary and Recommend Path.
